course: dictionary
lesson: 12743
title: Drumming: beat, sound and skill
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Drumming has three meanings. It can mean playing a drum: «Mia is drumming in the school band.» It can mean a steady beating or tapping sound: «The drumming of the rain kept me awake.» It can also mean the music or skill of playing drums: «Drumming is my favourite lesson.»
explain: To find the right meaning, look at the words around it. A band, a player or a lesson points to playing drums. Rain, a roof or a steady beat points to a tapping sound. Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Drumming can also show a feeling. «Tom kept drumming his fingers on the desk while he waited.» Tom is not playing music. The tapping shows he is impatient and wants to get going.
fact: Drumming is a verb (drum, drums, drummed, drumming) and a noun.
fact: «Drumming» can mean playing a drum, or a repeated beating or tapping sound.
fact: «Drumming» can also mean the music or skill of playing drums.
fact: Drumming is found in many cultures, such as African drumming, Japanese taiko and Irish bodhrán drumming.
fact: «Drumming your fingers» means tapping them, often because you are impatient or bored.
exercise: «The drumming of the rain kept Sam awake all night.» What does drumming mean here? | The skill of cooking | A loud shout | *A steady tapping or beating sound | Playing a drum in a band
exercise: «Ravi is learning drumming at the community centre.» What does drumming mean here? | *The music or skill of playing drums | A repeated tapping sound | Making a cake | Running very fast
exercise: «Lily kept drumming her fingers on the table while she waited.» What does the drumming show? | *Impatience | A cold day | Hunger | Happiness at a party
test: «The bodhrán is an Irish drum, and drumming on it is part of many folk tunes.» What is drumming here? | A sound of rain on a roof | Reading a book aloud | *Playing a drum to make music | Sitting still and quiet
test: Which phrase means tapping your fingers because you are impatient? | *Drumming your fingers | Drumming rain | Drum up support | Drum something into someone
exam: What word class is drumming in «The drumming of the waves was loud»? | A verb | *A noun | A conjunction | An adjective
